    "notes": "Profile of Arielle Kayabaga, Liberal MP for London West since 2021. Born in Bujumbura, Burundi circa 1990-1991; came to Canada as a refugee at age 11. First Black woman elected to London City Council (2018) and as MP in London (2021). Served briefly as Government House Leader and Minister of Democratic Institutions (March-May 2025) under PM Carney. Currently Deputy Government House Leader since June 2025. Re-elected with 56.30% in 2025. Educated at Carleton University (BA Political Science, 2013). Wikidata Q108628484.",
